Content provenance — Eita
=========================

Eita's curriculum (src/data/curriculum.json) is generated by
scripts/prepare-curriculum.mjs from source dumps in data/hanflow/, which were
copied from the HanFlow project (a Mandarin-learning dataset/app by the same
author, at ~/Desktop/HanFlow Home).

- Vocabulary lists derive from the official HSK 1–2 word lists (public
  information; word lists themselves are not copyrightable expression).
- Portuguese glosses, pinyin, grammar graph, exercises, and the moment/interest
  tagging come from HanFlow's own curated data and this repo's generator.
- The Eita code is MIT-licensed (see LICENSE). The MIT license covers the CODE
  ONLY — it does not grant rights over the bundled curriculum content.

Status: HanFlow carries no explicit license file. For the hackathon/demo scope
this is fine (same author, same machine). Before commercial distribution or a
public paid launch, add a LICENSE to the HanFlow source or get written
confirmation that the curriculum data may be redistributed — and update this
file accordingly.
